module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_cost_shape_claim_in_an_annotation_is_never_measured

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data a_cost_shape_claim_in_an_annotation_is_never_measured: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_cost_shape_claim_in_an_annotation_is_never_measured" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a source annotation asserted a cost shape for a routine -- that the reverse-closure walk in gunbc.regen_affected_set is linear in the edges -- and the routine was in fact quadratic in the set it reaches. The claim was written on 2026-11-09, when a cubic edge re-scan in that walk was removed; what remained was never measured.",

    "HOW IT WAS FOUND, on the fleet 2026-11-15 by reading run receipts rather than the annotation. The heal lane's regen scope round refused with MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash at memory.peak 26,873,634,816 bytes against the runner ceiling memory.high 26,843,545,600 bytes, elapsed_s 2547 and progress_marks 4, on a head changing 178 files (run 43700175877, job 132769446440); the same change family at 90 files refused the same way at 26,876,215,296 bytes and elapsed_s 2370 (run 43707054715, job 132790279664); an earlier head of the same family refused at 26,866,542,080 bytes after 2504513 ms of no progress (run 43689696985, job 132737591045). Heads whose bound answers Affected { members: [] } print that answer in about 9 s at memory.peak 16,050,896,896 and 16,065,765,376 bytes (runs 43702995862 and 43702268835).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Equal ceilings at unequal diff sizes -- 26.87 GB at 178 changed files and 26.88 GB at 90 -- rule out the diff size and name the reached set instead. The refusal carries no 'regen-emission-scope:' answer line, which localizes the cost to the scope phase, before any mirror is emitted. In the interpreter the Map value is Rc<HamtMap<..>> and shares structurally while the List value is a flat Rc<[Value]> slice, so a walk state carried in Lists pays a whole-array copy for every push and every skip: quadratic in what it accumulates.",

    "WHAT THE BROKEN SHAPE RUNS OVER, parsed from the tree at the drain head rather than read off a comment: 10,242 dag modules and 76,428 import edges. The in-degrees an importer accumulator is quadratic in: std.types 8,013 importers, std.algebra 2,592, std.live_tree 2,217, std.decl_ref 2,198, std.content_hash 2,161, std.ring 2,126, extdeps.external_authority 1,455. Accumulating each key's importers with list_push copies the backing array per insert -- the sum of deg^2/2 over keys, about 51M element copies per scoped round, paid whether or not the scope is empty, which is the floor under an empty-scope round.",

    "THE ANSWER SIZE IS WHAT DRAINS THE COST, NOT THE SIZE OF THE DIFF: the reverse closure from the 176 drained modules reaches 7,135 modules -- 70% of the corpus -- at depth 9, with 38,255 importer insertions. An 88-row drain closes onto essentially the same set, which is why a 90-file head and a 178-file head reach the same wall, while a head whose edited set reaches a handful of modules answers its scope round in about 9 s.",

    "PARTLY REPAIRED IN THE SAME CHANGE that records this mode: the walk carries { seen: Map, frontier: List } with level-synchronized rounds, the importer index is keyed instead of accumulated with list_push, the membership tests downstream read the keyed set, and each round's next frontier is built from that round's own importers rather than by re-scanning everything reached. No CI budget, runner ceiling, scope arm or host-side closure was touched. WHAT THE REPAIRED SHAPE COSTS IS UNREAD: with all of it in the tree the heal's scope round still refuses -- run 43732089173, job 132866555123, runner srv4-17, slot memory.high 26,843,545,600 B: emission scope 2,549 s, progress_marks 4, slot_memory_current 26,859,323,392 B by elapsed_s 727, 183,937 major faults/min, user CPU 19% of the wall, no answer line. The repair removes two quadratic terms; no run has established what a scoped round costs without them, so this row's rung stays unread.",

    "THE MODEL SIDE ALONE, measured locally under a hard 8 GB address-space cap with the CI-built interpreter (release-bins run 43662346030, sha256 e12a45db2f24135d2b76aabd4c21ce14b33af1f539cf1315667467d4680f82a9): a 30,443-edge subgraph harness -- three scope calls, closure 5,483 modules, edges and mirror rows passed as data literals -- runs in 229 s at 2,096,016 KiB peak before the repair and 223 s after it; a 76,428-edge harness with the 176 drained modules as the edited set -- the whole real import graph, the real answer size -- did not finish in 848 s at that cap before the repair, and with the repair in the model it completes: 814,227 ms of user CPU, peak resident 2,818,536 KiB, the claim passing. So the model's scope answer over the drain-shaped change costs under 3 GB, about a third of the time the heal's scope round spends, inside a cap an order of magnitude below the slot it fills: those numbers bound parsing plus model evaluation, and they do not account for the 26 GB above, which sits in the scope child's host-side work (the whole-corpus index it exists to hold, the edge index it builds before the model runs, and the second resolve it does for the lockstep check).",

    "WHY THE RUNG IS UNREAD, and what this mode refuses to leave behind: nothing in the corpus consumes a cost-shape sentence, so no control can tell whether a shape claim was measured -- the reading is ambiguous, not low. The ceiling this mode wants is a claim that names the run that established the shape, or says the shape is unread (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: the reported rung equals the rung established by executed evidence)."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.regen_affected_set", decl_name: "regen_reverse_closure", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.regen_affected_set", decl_name: "regen_closure_round", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.self_host_regen_affected_set_witness", decl_name: "a_reverse_closure_reaches_transitive_dependents_only", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
